 "blocks": [
  {
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Greek verbs fall into two conjugations, told apart by where the stress falls in the dictionary form (1st person singular). In the **first conjugation** the stress is on the stem: γράφω, διαβάζω, δουλεύω. This is the majority of verbs. In the second it is on the ending: αγαπώ, μπορώ (a later lesson).\n\nTo conjugate, take off the -ω and add the endings. The stress stays on the same syllable throughout."
  },
  {
   "type": "verb-paradigm",
